<biblStruct xml:id="b18">
	<monogr>
		<title level="m" type="main">Explanation: [Short and concise reason for assigning degree based on the corrected inconsistencies] ... &lt;|end_of_text|&gt; Ensure the output always ends with an &apos;&lt;|end_of_text|&gt;&apos; token and no inconsistency is repeated or added. {Examples} Now based on these examples, work for the following and remember to always end with an &apos;&lt;|end_of_text |&gt;&apos; token Input: {rough_analysis} Output: Listing 14: Result Prompt You are an evaluator tasked with analyzing inconsistencies in a chatbot&apos;s responses. You will receive an &apos;Analysis&apos; containing inconsistencies detected across multiple conversational turns</title>
		<imprint/>
	</monogr>
	<note>Second Inconsistency Reason for the inconsistency as given in Input] Degree of Inconsistency 1 to 5 Your goal is to generate a unified, concise list of inconsistencies covering the entire conversation while eliminating redundancy. Follow these guidelines</note>
